<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Egypt, North Africa and Sudan</p><h1 class="st-title">Vandal Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">435 CE – 534 CE · capital Carthage</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Germanic kingdom of the Vandals and Alans in North Africa, whose fleet sacked Rome in 455 and dominated the western Mediterranean.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/alans">Alans</a> crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> in 406 and entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 409. In 429 King Gaiseric led them across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-gibraltar">Strait of Gibraltar</a> into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. A treaty of 435 made them federates of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a>, but in 439 Gaiseric seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a>, taking <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/africa-proconsularis">Africa Proconsularis</a>, the richest western province.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gaiseric ruled as an independent king, confiscating Roman estates for his followers while keeping Roman administration and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> culture. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arian Christians</a> and at times persecuted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicene-christianity">Nicene</a> clergy, most harshly under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huneric">Huneric</a>. Their fleet took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corsican-republic">Corsica</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearics</a>, and in 455 sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berber-revolt">Berber revolts</a>, such as that of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-aures">Kingdom of the Aures</a>, cut away the interior.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 530 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gelimer">Gelimer</a> deposed the pro-Roman king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hilderic">Hilderic</a>, giving Justinian a pretext to invade. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belisarius">Belisarius</a> won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ad-decimum">Ad Decimum</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tricamarum">Tricamarum</a> in 533, and Gelimer surrendered in 534. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> became the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/praetorian-prefecture-of-africa">Praetorian Prefecture of Africa</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vandals">Vandals</a> vanished as a people.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/vandal-kingdom.jpg" alt="Vandal Kingdom" width="320" height="319"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:M%C3%BCnze_50_Denari_-_Gelimer_-_K%C3%B6nig_der_Vandalen_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>435 CE – 534 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Carthage</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gaiseric, Huneric, Gelimer</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Arian Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Vandalic, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/tunisia">Tunisia</a>, <a href="/countries/algeria">Algeria</a>, <a href="/countries/libya">Libya</a>, <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of the Vandals and Alans, Vandal Africa</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=484&amp;focus=vandal-kingdom" aria-label="Vandal Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4939 850 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Vandal Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5259 1106L5338 1239M5259 1106L5328 1276M5259 1106L5166 1122M5259 1106L5268 1140M5259 1106L5062 1084M5259 1106L5304 942M5259 1106L5709 970M5259 1106L5161 1159M5259 1106L5259 1106M5259 1106L5065 1017"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5338 1239h0M5328 1276h0M5166 1122h0M5268 1140h0M5062 1084h0M5304 942h0M5709 970h0M5161 1159h0M5259 1106h0M5065 1017h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5259 1106h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5259 1106h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Carthage. <a href="/atlas?year=484&amp;focus=vandal-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
